# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-spec: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
<folder_context path="spec">
<product_goal_and_intent name="language-independent schema 2">
Specify one Git component, one responsible A2A Agent Card reference, exports, optional surface,
and direct aliased dependencies with durable adapter selections. The standard does not assume
the Go reference implementation.
</product_goal_and_intent>
<data_structure name="manifest">
Unknown fields are invalid.
<field name="schema">Integer constant 2, required.</field>
<field name="component">Component, required.</field>
<field name="agent">Agent, optional. Init may omit it; an upstream dependency may not.</field>
<field name="dependencies">List of direct dependencies, optional.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="component">
<field name="id">Lowercase component identifier, required.</field>
<field name="description">Human-readable description, optional upstream data.</field>
<field name="repository">Canonical repository reference, optional.</field>
<field name="exports">List of exports, optional.</field>
<field name="surface">Safe repository-relative directory or exact '.', optional.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="export">
<field name="adapter">Adapter family, required.</field>
<field name="name">Platform-facing export name, required.</field>
<field name="path">Safe repository-relative export path, optional.</field>
<field name="checksum">Adapter-specific upstream checksum, optional; retained for Zig.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="agent">
<field name="name">Display name, optional and not an identity key.</field>
<field name="card">HTTPS URL or safe repository-relative A2A Agent Card path, required.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="dependency">
<field name="name">Consumer-local alias, required.</field>
<field name="git">Git source, required.</field>
<field name="ref">Requested branch, tag, or commit, optional before add resolves the default branch.</field>
<field name="path">Safe repository-relative manifest root, optional.</field>
<field name="bindings">Durable adapter selections, optional while authoring and populated by add.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="binding">
<field name="adapter">Adapter family, required.</field>
<field name="variant">Concrete executable/integration variant, required.</field>
<field name="export">Selected upstream export name, optional.</field>
<field name="path">Consumer-local materialization or integration path, optional.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="lock">
Unknown fields are invalid. It records successful local application, not a second declaration.
<field name="schema">Integer constant 2, required.</field>
<field name="dependencies">Map keyed by consumer-local alias, required.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="locked_dependency">
<field name="component">Upstream component id, required.</field>
<field name="git">Git source, required.</field>
<field name="ref">Requested ref, required.</field>
<field name="path">Safe repository-relative manifest root, optional.</field>
<field name="commit">Resolved 40-hex commit shared by every binding, required.</field>
<field name="manifest">SHA-256 digest of the upstream manifest at commit, required.</field>
<field name="bindings">Successfully applied durable bindings, required.</field>
<field name="agent">Locked agent reference with usable location and Git provenance, required.</field>
<field name="surface">Materialized surface Git tree identity, optional.</field>
</data_structure>
<data_structure name="locked_agent">
<field name="name">Display name, optional and not an identity key.</field>
<field name="declaredCard">HTTPS URL or safe path declared by the upstream manifest, required.</field>
<field name="card">Usable HTTPS URL or consumer-relative recoverable metadata path, required.</field>
<field name="commit">Resolved 40-hex commit containing the declaration and relative card bytes, required.</field>
</data_structure>
<acceptance_criteria>
Schemas, examples, reference prose, CLI parser, and Go model agree. Include native, polyglot,
submodule-only, submodule plus build integration, directory surface, surface '.', and distinct
aliases for equal repository basenames. Schema 1 examples are invalid migration fixtures only.
</acceptance_criteria>
</folder_context>

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

